            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0183" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg57"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A14/294: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Burton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-06-04"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1925</hi>—[(<hi
                                rendition="#italic">?</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >p.m.</hi>]</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>51. Department’s No. 50, June 3, 7 p.m., last paragraph. As result of my
                    consultation with the President you are authorized, if in your opinion it is
                    wise, to indicate that if powers represented at present Conference, as well as
                    other interested powers, feel that moment is opportune to take further steps in
                    this matter, the President will be glad to extend invitation as you suggest. As
                    I indicated in telegram referred to above, if the President should call a
                    further naval disarmament conference, he would probably make the other a part of
                    it as was done last time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
